            <ArticleTitle>An unusual case of neck pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>644-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/PEC.0b013e31828e9e60</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The complaint of nontraumatic neck pain in a pediatric patient without fever or any other symptoms is unusual and can be very challenging. We present the case of a 4-year-old boy with imaging consistent with a rare diagnosis. This report discusses this diagnosis as well as the utility of advanced imaging and laboratory evaluations in the presentation of pediatric neck pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
